  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Boli mnie",
     "texto": [
      "In **Boli mnie głowa** («my head hurts»), the body part is the subject and **mnie** means «me».",
      "English says «my head hurts», but Polish uses no possessive: **Boli mnie głowa**, not **Moja głowa boli**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Singular and plural",
     "texto": [
      "**Boli** goes with a body part in the singular: **Boli mnie ząb**.",
      "**Bolą** goes with a plural noun: **Bolą mnie plecy**; in Polish, «back» is a plural word, even though English says «my back»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Symptoms and gender",
     "texto": [
      "For some symptoms, **mam** + object is used: **Mam gorączkę**, «I have a fever».",
      "**Jestem chory** is said by a man and **Jestem chora** by a woman."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
